# Barkly Access — End-to-End Data Pipeline, Participant Identification, Collection, Deduplication and UI Integration Repair

## Critical objective

Barkly Access is currently failing to connect its modules properly.

The previous repair attempts did not resolve the problems. The UI remains unreliable, participant detection is incomplete, duplicate entries still occur, message collection does not correctly resolve both sides of conversations, and the modules are not consistently connected to the same data source.

This task is an end-to-end engineering repair.

Do not perform another isolated UI patch.

Do not build another disconnected implementation.

Inspect the existing repository, trace the complete data flow, identify the root causes, and implement a unified architecture connecting the collector, participant resolver, storage, deduplication, Frequent, Stats, collection popup and UI.

The project must use one consistent source of truth.

