# PHASE 5 — IMPLEMENT ROBUST DEDUPLICATION

Deduplication must be enforced across the entire pipeline.

## Message deduplication

Use reliable message identifiers and conversation scope where available.

Prevent:

- Duplicate messages within one batch.
- Duplicate messages across overlapping batches.
- Duplicate messages across sessions.
- Duplicate messages during retries.
- Duplicate message aggregation.

Do not deduplicate messages solely by their text.

Identical text can represent distinct messages.

## Participant deduplication

Use stable participant identifiers.

Prevent:

- Duplicate participants within one batch.
- Duplicate participants across batches.
- Duplicate participants across collection sessions.
- Duplicate participant storage records.
- Duplicate Frequent entries.

Do not deduplicate users by display name.

Two different users may have the same display name.

A user can change their display name or avatar without becoming a different user.

## Conversation deduplication

Use stable conversation identifiers.

Prevent duplicate conversation records and incorrect associations.

## Storage-level enforcement

Implement appropriate:

- Unique constraints.
- Upsert operations.
- Idempotent writes.
- Reconciliation of existing records.
- Safe duplicate cleanup.
- Integrity checks.

Deduplication must not exist only in the presentation layer.

Existing duplicate data should be reconciled safely where possible.

Preserve accurate message counts and relationships when merging duplicate records.

Do not destroy data during cleanup.

