# PHASE 6 — CONNECT FREQUENT TO THE SHARED DATA LAYER

Frequent must automatically populate from the shared participant and conversation data.

It must not have a separate collector.

It must not have a separate dataset.

It must not have its own independent identity-resolution logic.

## Frequent display

Display:

- Unique participants or conversation entries, according to the established identity scope.
- Name where available.
- Avatar where available.
- Aggregate message counts.
- Last interaction date where available.
- Other necessary non-content metadata.

## Frequent restrictions

Frequent must never display:

- Actual message contents.
- Message previews.
- Message snippets.
- Quotes.
- Attachments.
- AI-generated conversation summaries.

## Frequent functionality

- Search.
- Sorting.
- Accurate aggregated message counts.
- Correct participant association.
- Conversation navigation.
- Accessible rendering.
- Empty states.
- Error states.
- Loading states.

Clicking an entry must navigate to the corresponding Discord conversation through supported UI mechanisms.

Verify that Frequent updates when collection data changes.

